  "name": "KETONE (D3 HYDROXY BUTRATE RANBUT)",
  "code": "1125",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"244\"><strong data-start=\"206\" data-end=\"244\">Purpose and Clinical Significance:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"245\" data-end=\"761\">\n<li data-start=\"245\" data-end=\"363\">\n<p data-start=\"247\" data-end=\"363\">Measures <strong data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"299\">D-3-Hydroxybutyrate (&beta;-hydroxybutyrate)</strong>, the predominant ketone body in serum during states of ketosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"364\" data-end=\"518\">\n<p data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"518\">Useful in <strong data-start=\"376\" data-end=\"433\">diagnosing and monitoring diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA)</strong>, especially in diabetic patients with elevated blood glucose and metabolic acidosis.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"519\" data-end=\"610\">\n<p data-start=\"521\" data-end=\"610\">More specific and stable than traditional urine ketone tests (which detect acetoacetate).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"611\" data-end=\"761\">\n<p data-start=\"613\" data-end=\"761\">Helps in evaluating <strong data-start=\"633\" data-end=\"681\">fasting states, alcohol-induced ketoacidosis</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"686\" data-end=\"717\">inborn errors of metabolism</strong> involving ketone production or utilization.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>D-3 Hydroxybutyrate Levels</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Possible Clinical Indications</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Elevated</strong></td>\n<td>Diabetic ketoacidosis (DKA), prolonged fasting/starvation, alcoholism, low-carbohydrate diets, inborn errors of metabolism (e.g., fatty acid oxidation defects), pregnancy-related ketosis</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Normal or Low</strong></td>\n<td>Normal metabolic state, well-controlled diabetes, non-ketotic hyperglycemia</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
